---
import GovLayout from '../../layouts/GovLayout.astro';
import PhaseBanner from '../../components/PhaseBanner.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import InsetText from '../../components/InsetText.astro';
---
<GovLayout title="Arrest & Wanted System" department="Ministry of Justice" description="How the Wanted status, arrest mechanics, confiscation, and police progression work in ASEAN Motor Club.">

<PhaseBanner tag="Policy" text="Updated 27 April 2026" />
<Breadcrumbs items={[
  { label: "Justice & Law Enforcement", href: "/justice" },
  { label: "Arrest & Wanted System", href: "/justice/arrest-wanted" },
]} />

<main class="govuk-main-wrapper">
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <h1>Arrest & Wanted System</h1>

      <div class="govuk-notification-banner govuk-notification-banner--warning" role="region" aria-labelledby="critical-warning">
        <div class="govuk-notification-banner__wrapper">
          <h2 class="govuk-notification-banner__heading" id="critical-warning">
            Critical Warning
          </h2>
          <p><strong>Teleporting while Wanted triggers immediate automatic arrest.</strong> Do not teleport, reset your vehicle, or respawn until your Wanted status expires.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">What You Need to Know</h2>
      <div class="govuk-grid-row">
        <div class="govuk-grid-column-one-half">
          <div class="govuk-summary-list">
            <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__key">Criminal Record</span>
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__value">Created on illicit cargo load — permanent until arrested</span>
            </div>
            <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__key">Bounty</span>
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__value">Confiscatable amount — accumulates per delivery, decays with 2h half-life online</span>
            </div>
            <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__key">Wanted status</span>
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__value">Starts at 600 heat — expires in 10 minutes if avoiding police</span>
            </div>
            <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__key">Police within 500m</span>
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__value">Slows decay via 1/r² law; cannot fully expire</span>
            </div>
            <div class="govuk-summary-list__row">
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__key">On arrest</span>
              <span class="govuk-summary-list__value">All confiscatable money seized + 60 seconds in jail</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 id="criminal-record">1. Criminal Record</h2>
      <p>Loading illicit cargo creates an active <strong>Criminal Record</strong>, applies the <code>[C]</code> tag to your name, and begins accumulating two amounts:</p>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Criminal Record fields</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>amount</strong></td>
            <td>Permanent lifetime total of all illicit delivery payments on this record. Used for criminal level display. Never decays.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>confiscatable_amount</strong></td>
            <td>Also accumulates with deliveries but <strong>decays over time while you're online</strong>. This is what is seized on arrest. Sorted and displayed in <code>/wanted</code>.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>The Criminal Record is <strong>never cleared by time</strong>. It is only cleared on arrest, which immediately removes the <code>[C]</code> tag.</p>

      <InsetText>
        Only one active Criminal Record can exist per character at a time. A new record is created fresh after each arrest.
      </InsetText>

      <div class="govuk-inset-text">
        <strong>Example:</strong> If you deliver $50,000 of illicit cargo, your Criminal Record shows $50,000. After 2 hours of playing (staying online and active), this drops to $25,000. After 4 hours, it drops to $12,500. Decay pauses while AFK or in a modded vehicle.
      </div>

      <h2 id="bounty-confiscatable">2. Bounty / Confiscatable Amount</h2>
      <p>The term <strong>bounty</strong> refers to <code>CriminalRecord.confiscatable_amount</code>. This is the amount that accumulates from illicit deliveries and is seized on arrest.</p>

      <h3>Accumulation</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Every illicit delivery adds its payment value to <code>confiscatable_amount</code></li>
        <li>This is the same field that accumulates in the Criminal Record</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Decay</h3>
      <p>Your <code>confiscatable_amount</code> decays via exponential decay with a <strong>2-hour half-life of online time</strong>:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Formula: <code>confiscatable_amount *= 0.5 ^ (1/120)</code> per minute</li>
        <li>Only decays while the player is <strong>online</strong> (last_online within 60 seconds)</li>
        <li>Decay is <strong>paused</strong> if:
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>Player is AFK (<code>bAFK=true</code>)</li>
            <li>Player is in a modded vehicle (custom parts detected)</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>Amounts below $100 are zeroed out</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>On arrest</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>The current <code>confiscatable_amount</code> is seized</li>
        <li>The Criminal Record is then cleared</li>
      </ul>

      <InsetText>
        <strong>Proximity-based bounty growth was removed on 26 April 2026.</strong> The monetary <code>Wanted.amount</code> field is no longer used and remains $0. Only <code>confiscatable_amount</code> is seized on arrest.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="wanted-status">3. Wanted Status</h2>
      <p>Wanted is a temporary status that can be initiated in exactly <a href="#pursuit-initiation">two ways</a>: by an on-duty officer via <code>/setwanted</code>, or automatically upon <a href="#pursuit-initiation">illicit cargo delivery</a>.</p>

      <InsetText>
        <strong>30-second debounce window:</strong> Multiple deliveries within 30 seconds of each other are aggregated before the probability roll. Splitting large cargo into many small deliveries is treated as a single delivery of the combined value.
      </InsetText>

      <h3>Time-limited status — police proximity slows decay</h3>
      <p>All Wanted statuses begin at <strong>5 stars (600 heat)</strong>. Wanted heat decays at a <strong>constant rate of 1.0 heat/second</strong> when no police are nearby. A full W5 status (600 heat) expires naturally in <strong>10 minutes</strong> if you avoid all police.</p>
      <p>When an on-duty officer is within <strong>500 m</strong>, the server <em>reduces</em> the decay rate based on a <strong>1/r² law</strong> with a reference distance of 200 m. The closer the police, the slower your Wanted status expires. Decay never reverses — heat only ever decreases, never increases.</p>

      <div class="govuk-inset-text">
        <strong>Simple rule:</strong> Stay more than 500m away from all police officers and your Wanted status expires in 10 minutes. Get closer and it takes longer.
      </div>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>How long until Wanted expires by distance to nearest officer</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Distance to police</th><th>Time to expire</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>No police nearby</td><td>~10 minutes</td><td>Full speed escape</td></tr>
          <tr><td>500m or more away</td><td>~10 minutes</td><td>Full speed escape</td></tr>
          <tr><td>400m away</td><td>~12.5 minutes</td><td>Slightly slower</td></tr>
          <tr><td>300m away</td><td>~14.5 minutes</td><td>Moderately slower</td></tr>
          <tr><td>200m away</td><td>~20 minutes</td><td>Half speed</td></tr>
          <tr><td>100m away</td><td>~50 minutes</td><td>Very slow decay</td></tr>
          <tr><td>50m away (MIN_DISTANCE)</td><td>~110 minutes</td><td>Almost frozen</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10m away (point-blank)</td><td>~110 minutes</td><td>Almost frozen (capped at MAX_DECAY=10)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="govuk-notification-banner govuk-notification-banner--warning" role="region" aria-labelledby="cannot-expire-warning">
        <div class="govuk-notification-banner__wrapper">
          <h3 class="govuk-notification-banner__heading" id="cannot-expire-warning">
            Cannot Escape While Police Are Close
          </h3>
          <p>Wanted status <strong>cannot fully expire</strong> while any officer is within 500m — your heat is clamped at a minimum of <strong>0.1 heat</strong>, preventing the last sliver from reaching zero. Once all officers are beyond 500m, the restriction lifts and natural decay brings it to zero automatically.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Star indicator (***** — 1 to 5 stars)</h3>
      <p>Your Wanted severity is displayed as asterisk stars in your player tag, from <code>*</code> (1 star) to <code>*****</code> (5 stars). All Wanted statuses begin at <strong>5 stars (maximum heat, 600 heat units)</strong>. Stars are based on remaining heat with each band covering 120 units:</p>

      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Star level by remaining heat</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Stars in tag</th><th>Remaining heat</th><th>Display example</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">***** (max)</td><td>481 – 600</td><td><code>[*****C1] John</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">****</td><td>361 – 480</td><td><code>[****C1] John</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">***</td><td>241 – 360</td><td><code>[***C1] John</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">**</td><td>121 – 240</td><td><code>[**C1] John</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">*</td><td>1 – 120</td><td><code>[*C1] John</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">Expired</td><td>0</td><td><code>[C1] John</code> (stars removed)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>You receive an in-game system message each time your star level changes. When fully expired, you are notified and a server-wide announcement confirms your escape.</p>

      <h3>What happens when...</h3>
      
      <div class="govuk-details" data-module="govuk-details">
        <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
          <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">
            What happens when I load illicit cargo?
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="govuk-details__text">
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>You immediately get a Criminal Record [C] tag on your name (unless you are on police duty)</li>
            <li>If you are on police duty, the criminal record is <strong>not</strong> created</li>
            <li>A modded vehicle check is performed — if custom parts are detected, a warning popup is shown</li>
            <li>A smuggling tip-off may be broadcast to the server (see <a href="#smuggling-tipoff">Section 13</a>)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="govuk-details" data-module="govuk-details">
        <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
          <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">
            What happens when I deliver illicit cargo?
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="govuk-details__text">
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>You may become Wanted (higher delivery value = higher chance within 30s window)</li>
            <li>Money accumulates in your <code>CriminalRecord.confiscatable_amount</code> (the "bounty")</li>
            <li>Your criminal level increases based on cumulative laundered total</li>
            <li>On-duty police receive a risk premium bonus on Money deliveries</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="govuk-details" data-module="govuk-details">
        <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
          <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">
            What happens when police catch me?
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="govuk-details__text">
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>You're teleported to jail immediately</li>
            <li>Your <code>CriminalRecord.confiscatable_amount</code> is seized</li>
            <li>Your Criminal Record is cleared and [C] tag removed</li>
            <li>You're confined to jail for 60 seconds (cannot leave the area)</li>
            <li><strong>All online active (non-AFK) police officers receive an equal share</strong> of the confiscated amount. Each officer gets <code>confiscated_amount // active_officer_count</code> (minimum $1). Each officer also gets the full amount counted toward their police level progression.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="govuk-details" data-module="govuk-details">
        <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
          <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">
            What happens if I teleport while Wanted?
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="govuk-details__text">
          <div class="govuk-notification-banner govuk-notification-banner--warning">
            <div class="govuk-notification-banner__wrapper">
              <p class="govuk-notification-banner__heading">Immediate Automatic Arrest</p>
              <p>Teleporting while Wanted is treated as an attempt to evade capture. You are instantly arrested with full confiscation — same consequences as being caught by police.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>This includes:</p>
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>Manual teleport (via <code>/tp</code> command or menu)</li>
            <li>Using portals</li>
            <li>Vehicle reset (roadside recovery/Rescue)</li>
            <li>Respawning at hospital or garage</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="govuk-details" data-module="govuk-details">
        <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
          <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">
            What happens when I log out while Wanted?
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="govuk-details__text">
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>Your Wanted status persists — it does NOT clear</li>
            <li>When you log back in, your Wanted status resumes</li>
            <li><strong>If you log out within 2km of any on-duty officer, you are treated as arrested</strong> — full confiscation and jail time apply</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="govuk-details" data-module="govuk-details">
        <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
          <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">
            How do I escape Wanted status?
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="govuk-details__text">
          <p>To clear your Wanted status:</p>
          <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
            <li>Stay more than 500m away from ALL police officers</li>
            <li>Wait 10 minutes (do not teleport, respawn, reset vehicle, or enter portals)</li>
            <li>Do NOT log out near police (within 2km)</li>
            <li>Do NOT use modded vehicles (2-minute grace period, then auto-arrest)</li>
            <li>Do NOT go underwater (below z = -22455)</li>
            <li>Watch your star level decrease (W5 → W4 → W3 → W2 → W1 → Expired)</li>
          </ol>
          <p>Your Criminal Record [C] remains — only Wanted status expires. A future arrest will still clear it.</p>
          <p>Your <code>confiscatable_amount</code> (bounty) continues to decay while you're online and not AFK or in a modded vehicle.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 id="costumes-suspect">4. Criminal Costumes & Suspect System</h2>
      <p>Criminals wearing certain <strong>suspect costumes</strong> are flagged as suspects in-game, making them visible to police with a blue overlay on the police HUD. This system ensures criminals cannot hide by simply equipping a costume.</p>

      <h3>How it works</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>When a player with an active Criminal Record equips a <strong>suspect costume</strong>, they are immediately flagged as a suspect in-game</li>
        <li>When the costume is removed, the suspect flag is cleared immediately (unless the player is also Wanted)</li>
        <li>Wanted players are always flagged as suspects regardless of costume</li>
        <li>The suspect flag is refreshed every 10 seconds by the server to maintain consistency</li>
      </ul>

      <InsetText>
        Not all costumes trigger suspect status — only specific costumes configured by the server (e.g. <code>Costume_Butcher_01</code>) are classified as suspect costumes. Standard costumes do not trigger this system.
      </InsetText>

      <h3>Position hiding</h3>
      <p>Wanted players and on-duty police officers are <strong>hidden from player position streams</strong> to prevent metagaming:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Wanted criminals do not appear on other players' position maps</li>
        <li>On-duty police are hidden when any Wanted suspect is active</li>
        <li>Police can still see suspect locations via the <code>/suspects</code> command</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="pursuit-initiation">5. How Police Pursuit Is Initiated</h2>
      <p>Police pursuit (creating a Wanted status) is initiated in exactly <strong>two</strong> ways:</p>

      <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
        <li><strong><code>/setwanted</code> by an on-duty officer</strong> — see <a href="#setwanted">Section 6</a> for full details.</li>
        <li><strong>Illicit cargo delivery</strong> (Money, Ganja, Cocaine, etc.) — a probability roll based on accumulated value within a 30-second debounce window:
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li><strong>10% floor chance</strong> on any delivery</li>
            <li><strong>100% at $100,000 or more</strong></li>
            <li>Scales linearly between the floor and cap</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <InsetText>
        <strong>Pull-over penalties do NOT create Wanted status.</strong> The police pull-over system performs an immediate arrest if the suspect already has an active Criminal Record and the officer issues a penalty (not a warning). It never applies a new Wanted status.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="setwanted">6. <code>/setwanted</code> Command</h2>
      <p>On-duty police officers can manually flag a player as Wanted using <code>/setwanted &lt;name&gt;</code>:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Requires on-duty police</strong> (<code>/police</code> active)</li>
        <li><strong>Target must be online</strong> and not AFK</li>
        <li><strong>Cannot use on yourself</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Cannot use on already-Wanted players</strong></li>
        <li><strong>30-minute cooldown</strong> from the target's last Wanted expiry — shows exact minutes and seconds remaining</li>
        <li><strong>1km minimum distance</strong>: If any officer is within 1km of the target when <code>/setwanted</code> is issued, those officers are <strong>despawned and teleported</strong> to the nearest police station outside the 1km radius</li>
        <li><strong>Innocence warning</strong>: If the target has no active Criminal Record, the officer gets a "WARNING: No recent illicit activity detected" note but can still proceed</li>
        <li>Sets Wanted to <strong>600 heat (5 stars)</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="police-duty">7. Police Duty & Commands</h2>

      <h3><code>/police</code> — Toggle police duty</h3>
      <p>Going on duty has several requirements and effects:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Cannot go on duty while Wanted</strong></li>
        <li><strong>24-hour crime cooldown</strong>: Cannot go on duty within 24 hours of committing a crime (any illicit delivery linked to a Criminal Record)</li>
        <li><strong>Must be on foot</strong> — cannot activate while in a vehicle</li>
        <li><strong>Teleported to nearest police station</strong> on activation (away from any Wanted suspects)</li>
        <li>A server-wide announcement is broadcast when you go on or off duty</li>
      </ul>

      <h3><code>/suspects</code> (or <code>/s</code>) — List wanted suspects</h3>
      <p>On-duty officers can view all online Wanted suspects with distance and compass bearing:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Shows each suspect's name, distance, and direction</li>
        <li>Sorted by distance (closest first)</li>
        <li>Requires on-duty police status</li>
      </ul>

      <h3><code>/wanted</code> — List all wanted criminals</h3>
      <p>Anyone can view the full wanted list, which shows three sections:</p>
      <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
        <li><strong>Active Bounties</strong> — Wanted suspects with star levels and confiscatable amounts, sorted online first then by bounty</li>
        <li><strong>Recently Wanted</strong> — Suspects on cooldown from recent Wanted expiry</li>
        <li><strong>Criminal Record</strong> — Players with active records but no Wanted status, showing criminal level, bounty, and decay rate</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="police-teleport">8. Police Teleport Restrictions</h2>
      <p>Several teleport restrictions apply to both wanted suspects and on-duty officers:</p>

      <h3>Wanted criminals</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Cannot teleport</strong> via <code>/tp</code>, <code>/tp vehicle</code>, <code>/tp coords</code>, or game teleport/respawn/vehicle-reset</li>
        <li>Attempting any of these triggers <strong>immediate auto-arrest</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h3>On-duty police</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Cannot teleport within 1km of wanted suspects</strong> — any teleport destination is checked; blocked with a popup if too close</li>
        <li><strong>Teleport/respawn redirect</strong>: If an on-duty officer teleports or respawns and lands within 1km of a wanted suspect, they are <strong>automatically teleported to the nearest police station</strong> with a system message</li>
        <li><strong>Restricted locations</strong>: Dasa and Harbor teleport points are blocked while on duty</li>
        <li><strong>Custom destination teleport blocked</strong> for police on duty</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="police-conduct">9. Police Conduct & Arrest Procedure</h2>
      <p>Police officers must follow the correct procedure before initiating pursuit. Skipping steps or targeting ineligible players is considered misconduct.</p>

      <div class="govuk-grid-row">
        <div class="govuk-grid-column-one-half">
          <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">What police CAN do</h3>
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--tick">
            <li>Stop and question players with [C] tag</li>
            <li>Use <code>/setwanted</code> on suspects (30-minute cooldown after expiry)</li>
            <li>Pursue uncooperative suspects</li>
            <li>Receive equal share of confiscated money on any arrest</li>
            <li>Use <code>/suspects</code> to track wanted players</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="govuk-grid-column-one-half">
          <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">What police CANNOT do</h3>
          <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--cross">
            <li>Use <code>/setwanted</code> on themselves or already-Wanted players</li>
            <li>Teleport within 1km of wanted suspects</li>
            <li>Teleport to Dasa or Harbor while on duty</li>
            <li>Use custom destination teleport while on duty</li>
            <li>Use the deprecated <code>/arrest</code> command</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3>Required procedure</h3>
      <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
        <li><strong>Signal the suspect to stop and pull over.</strong> Use lights, sirens, or in-game voice/chat to make the request clear.</li>
        <li><strong>Allow a reasonable opportunity to comply.</strong> Give the suspect time to react before beginning a pursuit.</li>
        <li><strong>Only pursue and arrest uncooperative suspects.</strong> If the suspect pulls over and complies, engage through roleplay — not immediate arrest. Arrests are reserved for suspects who flee or refuse to stop.</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="govuk-inset-text">
        <strong>Reporting misconduct:</strong> If an officer fails to follow this procedure — such as instantly arresting a compliant suspect — this may be a roleplay violation. Report incidents through the official channels.
      </div>

      <h2 id="arrest-mechanisms">10. Arrest Mechanisms</h2>
      <p>The <code>/arrest</code> command is <strong>deprecated</strong> and returns:</p>
      <blockquote>
        "/arrest is no longer available. Suspects are now arrested automatically when they log out near police, enter restricted zones, or use modded vehicles."
      </blockquote>
      <p>All arrests are now handled automatically through the following triggers:</p>

      <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
        <li><strong>Teleport / Respawn / Vehicle Reset while Wanted</strong> — Immediate auto-arrest</li>
        <li><strong>Portal Entry while Wanted</strong> — Auto-arrest when entering a portal</li>
        <li><strong>Logout near Police</strong> — If within 2km of any on-duty officer, logout is treated as arrest</li>
        <li><strong>Underwater</strong> — Wanted suspects below z = -22455 are auto-arrested</li>
        <li><strong>Modded Vehicle</strong> — Wanted suspects in modded vehicles are auto-arrested after a 2-minute grace period</li>
        <li><strong>Police Pull-Over Penalty</strong> — Suspects with an active Criminal Record are arrested immediately when an on-duty officer issues a penalty (not a warning). Warnings do not trigger arrest.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="confiscation">11. Confiscation</h2>
      <p>On arrest, the current <code>CriminalRecord.confiscatable_amount</code> is confiscated.</p>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>What is confiscated on arrest</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Criminal Record confiscatable amount</td>
            <td><code>CriminalRecord.confiscatable_amount</code> — accumulates from deliveries, decays over time while online</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p><strong>Total confiscation = CriminalRecord.confiscatable_amount</strong></p>

      <InsetText>
        There is no partial confiscation based on star level. If you are arrested at W1 or W5, the same full <code>confiscatable_amount</code> is seized.
      </InsetText>

      <h3>What happens to confiscated money</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>Deducted from the suspect's wallet</strong> via the mod server</li>
        <li><strong>Recorded as Treasury income</strong> under "Police Confiscation"</li>
        <li><strong>The suspect's criminal laundered total is reduced</strong> by the confiscated amount</li>
        <li><strong>All online active (non-AFK) police officers receive an equal share</strong> of the confiscated amount. Each officer gets <code>confiscated_amount // active_officer_count</code> (minimum $1). Each officer also gets the full amount counted toward their police level progression.</li>
        <li>A <strong>Confiscation record</strong> is permanently created, linking the suspect, officers, and amount</li>
        <li>The <strong>Criminal Record is cleared</strong> and the <code>[C]</code> tag is immediately removed</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>No Wanted = arrest still possible</h3>
      <p>If a player has an active Criminal Record (<code>[C]</code> tag) but no active Wanted status, they can still be arrested (teleported to jail and Criminal Record cleared). Only the <code>confiscatable_amount</code> is seized.</p>

      <h2 id="jail-containment">12. Jail Containment</h2>
      <p>When a player is arrested — by any auto-arrest trigger — they are immediately teleported to the designated <strong>Jail</strong> location. A <strong>60-second boundary enforcement</strong> period then begins automatically.</p>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Jail containment parameters</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Boundary radius</td><td>10 metres from the jail marker</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Enforcement duration</td><td>60 seconds after arrest</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Check frequency</td><td>Every second</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Teleport on escape</td><td>Immediate — vehicles are despawned</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>During the 60-second window, if the player moves more than <strong>10 metres</strong> from the jail marker, the server <strong>instantly teleports them back</strong> and shows a warning popup. This repeats on every tick until the containment period expires.</p>

      <InsetText>
        After 60 seconds the containment ends automatically and the player is free to move. There is no manual release step — the timer is enforced server-side and cannot be shortened.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="security-bonus">13. Security Risk Bonus</h2>
      <p>When active police officers are online, illicit delivery payments are increased to reflect the higher risk. Each on-duty officer adds <strong>50% to the base payout</strong>, capped at <strong>+250%</strong> (with 5 or more officers).</p>

      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Risk bonus by number of active officers</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Active officers</th><th>Bonus on delivery</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">0</td><td>+0%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">1</td><td>+50%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">2</td><td>+100%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">3</td><td>+150%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">4</td><td>+200%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">5+</td><td>+250% (maximum)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="police-progression">14. Police Progression</h2>
      <p>Officers advance in level based on their cumulative confiscated amount. Every <strong>$50,000 confiscated</strong> increases the officer's level by 1. When an officer levels up, their player tag is refreshed and a server-wide announcement is broadcast.</p>

      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Police level thresholds</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Cumulative confiscated</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">1</td><td>$0 – $49,999</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">2</td><td>$50,000 – $99,999</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">3</td><td>$100,000 – $149,999</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left"><em>N</em></td><td><em>(N − 1) × $50,000</em> onwards</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="smuggling-tipoff">15. Smuggling Tip-Offs</h2>
      <p>When a player loads illicit cargo, the system may broadcast a server-wide tip-off: <em>"Intelligence reports suggest a smuggling operation is underway"</em>. This is controlled by the <code>SMUGGLING_TIPOFF_ENABLED</code> server setting.</p>

      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Tip-off parameters</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Delay before broadcast</td><td>15 seconds</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cooldown per player</td><td>60 seconds</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <InsetText>
        Tip-offs do not reveal the player's name or location — they only alert police that a smuggling operation is in progress.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="modded-vehicles">16. Modded Vehicle Rules</h2>
      <p>Players using vehicles with custom-modified parts face additional penalties during illicit cargo gameplay:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li><strong>On delivery:</strong> Criminal profits are zeroed out (transferred back as a penalty) if modded parts are detected on the player's active vehicle.</li>
        <li><strong>On load:</strong> A warning popup is shown: "You are not allowed to use modified vehicles for criminal gameplay."</li>
        <li><strong>Police exception:</strong> On-duty officers with police-issued whitelisted parts are exempt from modded vehicle detection.</li>
      </ul>

    </div>
